ts/_shared/skills/powder/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":2832,"output":391,"cacheRead":5745,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":279,"totalTokens":8968,"cost":{"input":0.0026904,"output":0.0015639999999999999,"cacheRead":0.0009192,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0051736}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788551754973,"responseId":"gen-1788551755-bI7ZGeT9BfBPcxV5IRQt","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06dfdff7d72e384f2b4e040b53979","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: powder\ndescription: >\n  Powder is the exclusive-work ledger. Use when listing takeable jobs\n  for this repository, taking a job, asking the operator, or completing\n  work with proof after an approve Gate.\n---\n\n# Powder\n\nPowder stores jobs. Take one. Finish it. Write proof.\n\n## Client contract\n\nOrigin resolves from `POWDER_URL`, then `~/.config/powder/config`; there is no\ndefault. Remote origins require HTTPS; HTTP is loopback-only. `POWDER_AGENT` is\noptional audit metadata. Managed workers pass the\nexact canonical label `forest-misty-step/powder`, but this label never\nauthorizes a lease or any other operation. `POWDER_API_KEY` is transport\nauthentication.\n\nRun `powder doctor [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]` before selection to verify the\nconfigured origin and service. If the check fails, do not call Powder. GitHub\nIssues remain the Tracker.\n\nEach successful `powder take` returns a flat JSON Job plus a per-job\n`claim_token` made from 32 random bytes encoded as base64url. Only its SHA-256\nhash is stored in `jobs.lease_token_hash`. A live job returns `held` unless\nthe CLI presents that job's matching stored claim, which resumes it. An audit\nlabel never grants resume. The claim token is capability for only that lease.\n\nThe CLI stores claim tokens privately under XDG state by validated origin and\njob id, resumes by job id, and sends them automatically. It never prints\nclaims, and list/show/logs/notes never expose them. `release`, `renew`, `ask`,\n`done`, live-job field edits, and live `abandon` require the claim; missing is\n`claim_required`, and mismatch or expiry is `invalid_claim`. `note` stays\nreport-authorized and claim-independent. Free-job patching or abandon uses\n`promote` authority without a claim. Tokens are deleted after release, ask,\ndone, or abandon.\n\n## Factory loop\n\n1. When `POWDER_AGENT` is set, run\n   `powder list --mine \"$POWDER_AGENT\" --repo <forest.yaml repo>`. Treat\n   `--mine` as an audit-label filter, never as resumable authority. A live\n   candidate is resumable only when `powder take <id> [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]`\n   succeeds with the private claim stored for this origin and job id, and no\n   `forest/<id>/*` branch exists. When `POWDER_AGENT` is unset, attempt\n   resumption only for a job id supplied by the managed run or current branch;\n   otherwise continue to takeable selection.\n2. `powder list --takeable --repo <forest.yaml repo>`\n3. `powder show <id>`\n   The spec is the work. Empty spec is not takeable. Show never contains a\n   claim token.\n4. `powder take <id> [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]`\n   Do this before creating a branch. A successful take stores the private\n   claim. A live job returns `held`, even under the same audit label; do not\n   interpret `held` as permission from the label. Keep a published Subject\n   held for the Kernel completion loop, and release only a failed or\n   unpublished Builder attempt.\n5. A Fixer uses the same Subject's private claim by job id before branch\n   mutation; the audit label is only metadata.\n6. Publish with schema v2, `tracker` set to the source actually selected\n   (`github` or `powder`), and branch `forest/<id>/<slug>`. Every Subject uses\n   that shape, including GitHub Issue numbers.\n7. Agents do not call `powder done`. The Kernel completes the current\n   Git-landed Subject only when request evidence has `tracker: powder`, using\n   the approved Revision as proof. The CLI clears the private claim after\n   completion or any release/ask/abandon.\n\nMultiple distinct jobs may be held under the same managed audit label. Every\nclaim authorizes only its own job; managed workers and the Kernel do not mint\nor share authority from the label.\n\n\n## Verbs\n\n```\npowder list --takeable --repo REPO\npowder list --mine AGENT --repo REPO\npowder show ID\npowder take ID\npowder release ID\npowder ask ID --question '...'\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788551758050},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01a06dfe02427fc3be1fd117cbb2f45e","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"powder list --takeable --repo misty-step/canopy 2>&1; echo \"EXIT:$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":1340,"output":67,"cacheRead":8561,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":9968,"cost":{"input":0.0012729999999999998,"output":0.000268,"cacheRead":0.00136976,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00291076}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788551758050,"responseId":"gen-1788551758-D24UYk6ixVJgcnEWSkh8","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06dfe02427fc3be1fd117cbb2f45e","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-critic-discovery-id-collision\",\n    \"title\": \"Discovery ID collisions silently drop discoverable Forest instances\",\n    \"spec\": \"Problem: discovery deduplicates roots but generates IDs with sanitizeID; names such as agent_test and agent-test both become agent-test. Reconciliation keys workers/state by ID, so distinct roots can silently collapse or swap targets across scans.\\n\\nOutcome: discovered instances with distinct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.828Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: discovery.go:16 keys discovered candidates by root path, so DiscoverLocalInstances can return multiple instances whose sanitized IDs collide: sanitizeID (discovery.go:196-210) maps \\\"agent_test\\\" and \\\"agent-beta\\\" style names to the same ID (both \\\"agent-test\\\", underscores and dashes both normalize to \\\"-\\\"). app.go:239-241 then builds discMap keyed by instance ID, so the second colliding instance silently overwrites the first in the map and, at app.go:275-283, is skipped via existingMap — a working Forest checkout simply never appears in the fleet, with no log or error. The same silent-drop applies if a discovered ID matches an explicit inventory ID.\\nRequired: every discoverable, validated instance must either appear in the fleet or its omission must be surfaced; discovery IDs must be unique per instance or collisions must be resolved deterministically and observably.\\nProposed spec direction: make DiscoverLocalInstances deduplicate or disambiguate by ID (e.g. suffix the ID from the root path on collision) before returning, or make syncDiscoveredInstances log/record dropped collisions; add a discovery test with two sibling dirs whose names sanitize to the same ID.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Problem: discovery deduplicates roots but generates IDs with sanitizeID; names such as agent_test and agent-test both become agent-test. Reconciliation keys workers/state by ID, so distinct roots can silently collapse or swap targets across scans.\\n\\nOutcome: discovered instances with distinct normalized roots must not silently share an effective identity. Resolve collisions deterministically before worker/state reconciliation, preserving stable route-to-root binding across repeated scans and input order changes. Existing explicit inventory IDs and routes remain authoritative; do not overwrite or remove explicit entries. Preserve ordinary noncolliding IDs. Surface any instance intentionally omitted because of an explicit route conflict rather than presenting it as independently observed. Choose the smallest identity representation; no durable store or new coordinator.\\n\\nProof: deterministic fixtures for agent_test and agent-test at distinct roots show both discoverable instances retained with distinct valid IDs, stable on reordered scans, and no snapshots or workers attributed to the wrong root. Include discovered-versus-explicit collisions and existing explicit inventory preservation tests. Exercise fleet selection for each resolved instance. Correct original draft example: agent_test and agent-beta do not collide; agent_test and agent-test do.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.665Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:46:20.447Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": false,\n      \"takeable\": true\n    }\n  }\n]\nEXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788551759919},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01a06dfe09bc7711891c8179bfed5705","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"gh issue list --repo misty-step/canopy --label \"forest:ready\" --state open --limit 20 2>&1; echo \"EXIT:$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"meta/muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":1224,"output":78,"cacheRead":9841,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":11143,"cost":{"input":0.0011627999999999999,"output":0.000312,"cacheRead":0.00157456,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00304936}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788551759920,"responseId":"gen-1788551759-H3cWZpnUKqqsCGjfKNWn","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06dfe09bc7711891c8179bfed5705","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"EXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788551761626},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking eligibility by verifying remote branch emptiness, PR absence, and held job branch status before selection.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.summary\",\"summary\":\"Checking eligibility by verifying remote branch emptiness, PR absence, and held job branch status before selection.\",\"format\":\"meta-responses-v1\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"Q-PaDgGlx4tQgsmVjUKQeSClZWK9TKpMdLXdPN5sfcToeKLMqz74qAwHCZ8yQRS_iMX8-Ff0ldO6x3LBHAHVeYQzCpft2osE1oy8kqaUNuUB